WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.435
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.836
Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:04.938
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.773
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.175
Well, guys, yesterday,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.644
President Trump did an interview
with "60 Minutes,"

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.713
and it didn't go
exactly as planned.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.947
Take a look.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.984 line:0%
-President Trump abruptly ended
a solo interview

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.552 line:0%
with CBS's "60 Minutes,"

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.954 line:0%
and the President
did not return to the room

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:25.024 line:0%
for a joint interview
with Vice President Mike Pence.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.927 line:0%
President Trump sat down
with CBS News' Lesley Stahl

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.463 line:0%
for 45 minutes
before getting up and leaving

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.998 line:0%
and telling CBS that he thought
they had enough material.

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:34.266
[ Light laughter ]
-Ooh.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:36.569
-Hm.
-Yeah. Trump bailed early.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.570
He was like,
"I gave them 45 minutes.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.007
What else did '60 Minutes'
expect?"

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:44.444
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.712
It's "60 Minutes."

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.480
What level of questions
did he want?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.683
"So, how long have you been
so awesome for so long, dude?"

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.585
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.154
When Trump no-showed, Mike Pence
was like, "I'll still talk."

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:58.157
Lesley Stahl was like, "Uh,
I think we have enough footage."

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.626
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.127
"Yeah. Yeah, we got enough."

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.895
If you're keeping score,
Trump's attacked

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.698
"60 Minutes," doctors,
and the Postal Service.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.466
At this point, seniors are like,

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:09.002
"Do you want us
to vote for you or not?

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.037
Just tell us.
We don't have to."

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.404
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:13.873
Seriously, if you're trying
to win the senior vote,

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.875
you can't insult "60 Minutes."

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.611
That's like trying to win the
youth vote by banning TikTok.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.446
Oh, wait, he did that, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.215
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.549
Apparently, Trump was annoyed

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:25.150
'cause his segment
was going to air

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.354
after the one about a guy who
carves rodeo stars out of soap.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.790
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.626 --> 00:01:36.362
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.730
Oh, man.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.365
There's a producer
at "60 Minutes"

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.568
really laughing at that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.736
Well, after that,
Trump held a campaign rally

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.438
in Erie, Pennsylvania,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.173
where he sounded pretty thrilled

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.407
about the "60 Minutes"
interview.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:49.576
Listen to this.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.978 line:0%
-You have to watch what we do
to "60 Minutes."

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.213 line:0%
You'll get
such a kick out of it.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.882 line:0%
You're going to
get a kick out of it.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:59.418 line:0%
Lesley Stahl
is not going to be happy.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:02.755
-Yeah. Yeah. He looked like
he really got a kick out of it.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.024
Here he is immediately
after the interview.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.192
This is real.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.962
-Yeah.
[ Helicopter blades whirring ]

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.264
-Wow.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.266
[ Whirring continues ]
-Oh.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:17.170
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.637
-He looks like Rudy Giuliani
on his way

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:20.206
to the "Borat" premiere.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.442
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.243
[ Applause ]

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:28.548
♪♪

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.349
♪♪

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:31.684
-♪ Borat ♪

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:35.054
-Uh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.689
But at that rally,
Trump didn't seem too excited --

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:38.957
this is...
[laughs]

00:02:38.957 --> 00:02:40.593
this is real, by the way.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.295
He didn't seem too excited
to be in Erie, Pennsylvania.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:44.464 line:0%
Check this out.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.799 line:0%
-Before the plague came in,
I had it made.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.902 line:0%
I wasn't coming to Erie.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.403 line:0%
I mean, I have to be honest.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.071 line:0%
There's no way I was coming.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.807
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.810
-Everyone in the crowd
was like...

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.645
"Yeah, r-right?

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:03.283
There's no way he would have
come to see us, right?"

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.650
That's quite a message, huh?

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.586
He's like,
"I'm only here with you losers

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.520
in your loser town
because I'm losing."

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.922
[ Laughter ]
"So I guess

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.557
we're all a bunch of losers
except for me.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.592
I'm the winner."

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.493
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.362
It's like showing up
at someone's party and saying,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.164
"I'm only here because
things are bad at home."

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.299
I just..."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:23.135
"I don't even care
if you talk to me."

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.072
"This whole place is a dumpster.
Anyway, vote for me."

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.240
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.141
Well, guys,
with less than two weeks left

00:03:29.141 --> 00:03:30.376
until Election Day,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.178
candidates are making
their closing arguments

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.779
to really drive home
their message.

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:34.947
Here's one from Trump.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.984
♪♪

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.618 line:0%
-They said, "Would you
like to wear a hat?"

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.654 line:0%
I said, "There's no way
I'm wearing a hat."

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.823
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:46.993
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.530
-"'Do you want to wear a hat?'

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.532
I said, 'There's no way
I'm wearing that hat.'"

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.333
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.135
[ Chuckling ] Okay.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.637
[ Laughs ]

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:01.006
Meanwhile,
on the Democratic side today,

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:04.009
President Obama finally returned
to the campaign trail

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.778
to support Joe Biden.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.713
It's like that moment when
you've canceled on your friend

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:09.315
so many times,
you have to make up for it

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.716
by going to
a really long brunch.

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:14.353
[ Laughter ]
"So your kid's 5 now, huh?

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.956
That's cool."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.824
Don't worry --
Trump has a response to this.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:20.760
Tomorrow, Dean Cain
will be greeting people

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.662
outside a Des Moines Jiffy Lube.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.431
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.932
How about another
closing argument from Trump?

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.000
Do we have one?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.703
♪♪

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.505 line:0%
-Does anybody have
a little sunblock?

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.041 line:0%
I'd love to use it right now.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.810 line:0%
I'm always preaching to my kids,
sunblock, sunblock,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.011 line:0%
and here I am like an idiot.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:40.379
♪♪

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.014
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:45.317
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.585
-"They want me to wear a hat.

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.821
I said,
'I'm not wearing a hat.'"

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.390
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.128
"You guys like...?"

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.496
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.764
What?

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.833
[ Chuckling ]
What's going on?

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.067
Here's some
entertainment news --

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.703
normally, around this time
of year, we start seeing

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.972
all the classic Charlie Brown
holiday specials on TV.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.608
But this season, it's going
to be a little different.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.776
Take a look.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:13.012 line:0%
-For the first time
in more than 50 years,

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.814 line:0%
Charlie Brown's holiday specials

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.616 line:0%
will not be broadcast
on network TV.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:19.585 line:0%
From now on, iconic shows like

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.620 line:0%
"It's the Great Pumpkin,
Charlie Brown"

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.422 line:0%
and "A Charlie Brown Christmas"

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.791 line:0%
can only be seen on Apple TV+.

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:27.259
-Boo. Boo.
-Boo.

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.895
-Nothing like teaching kids
the true meaning of the holidays

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.464
by forcing them
to cough up money

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:35.034
to watch a 54-year-old cartoon.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.535
Even worse,
they told Charlie Brown

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:37.803
it was going to be on TV

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.772
and then pulled it away
at the last second.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:40.939
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:44.376
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:48.213
[ Muffled gibberish ]

00:05:48.213 --> 00:05:49.682
It's kind of a weird move.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.385
I mean, who was like, "I was
holding out on buying Apple TV,

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:57.390
but now...I have no choice.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.960
I cave."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.463
"I've got to -- got to see my
Charlie Brown holiday specials."

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.232
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:10.036
"I was saving up
to send the kids to school..."

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.304
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:14.873
"No.

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:17.142
No school.

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:18.411
Charlie Brown's school."

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:22.748
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.249
Some more TV news --

00:06:24.249 --> 00:06:26.952
last night was an all-new
episode of "The Bachelorette."

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.955
I love "The Bachelorette," man.
-Whoo! Whoo!

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:32.491
-It seemed like one of the group
dates got off to a rough start

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:36.562
when nobody asked Clare to go --
to go talk one-on-one.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.097
You know they have to do
the one-on-ones?

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.431 line:0%
Watch this.
It's awkward.

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.634 line:0%
-[ Sighs ]

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:46.472 line:0%
[ Sighs ] So...
should we get the night started?

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.773 line:0%
-I think we should.
-Yeah.

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:50.075 line:0%
-We should.
-Yeah?

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:53.278 line:0%
Alright.
Does anybody want to...

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:55.747 line:0%
[ Clears throat ]
-Yeah. Let's do it.

00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:57.216 line:0%
-...step up to the plate?

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.917 line:0%
-I would love to -- I would love
to go chat with you.

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:00.052 line:0%
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.488
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:06.158
-"So, um..."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:09.228
"...guys, uh -- right? --
you want to get it --

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:12.064
you want to get
it going here or, uh...

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.533
You know, anyone can, you know,
just jump in when you feel it."

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.936
[ Laughter ]
"Anyone?

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:18.904
In no particular order,
of course."

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:21.173
[ Laughter ]
"I'll close my eyes.

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:22.875
Whoever grabs my hand first
is the one."

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.310
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:28.681
"Just forget the hand thing.
Let's just, you know, decide.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.749
Pointing at you."

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.784
"I'd like to start a chat."

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:35.087
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:37.756
Actually, that wasn't the most
awkward moment of the night,

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:39.191
'cause, later on,
all the guys played

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.127
a game of strip dodgeball.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.127
Take a look.

00:07:42.127 --> 00:07:43.428 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:43.428 --> 00:07:44.730 line:0%
-Whoo-hoo!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.999 line:0%
-Blue team,
take off your shorts.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:49.401 line:0%
-Blue team!
Off with your shorts.

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:50.803 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.671 line:0%
-Demar is out.

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:55.007 line:0%
So, player, this is it
for the blue team.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.776 line:0%
They're taking
the walk of shame home.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:02.114
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.849
-[ Voice breaking ] I'm sorry.
I'm a little emotional.

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:07.153
Um, naked dodgeball is how
my grandparents met.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.387
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.387 --> 00:08:11.023
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.825
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.728
Hey, do we have any more
closing arguments from Trump?

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:16.829
We have one more.

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:19.098
♪♪

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:21.166 line:0%
-Women.

00:08:21.166 --> 00:08:22.268 line:0%
I like women.

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.569
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:24.970
-Ah!

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.106
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:30.509
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.511
-And finally, get this --
a town in Canada

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:34.146
has decided to change its name.

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:36.014
Check out what it's been
called until now.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:39.384 line:0%
-The Canadian town has
rid itself of its toxic name.

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:42.555 line:0%
-For 120 years, it was
officially called Asbestos.

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:44.623 line:0%
It was proudly named
for its asbestos mine,

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:48.760 line:0%
but after years of ridicule,
the city has been rebranded.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:49.861
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:08:49.861 --> 00:08:52.030
Now the only asbestos town left

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.832
is at the New Jersey Six Flags.

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:56.802
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:59.005
-Yeah, the new name
will really help its reputation

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:00.339
according to the town mayor,

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.674
Steve Hepatitis.

